# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plugging into ffsim’s simulation interface {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"
msgstr "Pagsaksak sa simulation interface ng ffsim {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) is a high-performance simulator for fermionic quantum circuits that exploits particle number and spin-Z conservation to represent state vectors more compactly than a generic $2^n$-dimensional qubit statevector. It defines protocols that any object can implement to participate in its simulation machinery (see [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for this package’s own protocols, which follow the same design):\n"
msgstr "Ang [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) ay isang high-performance na simulator para sa mga fermionic quantum circuit na sinasamantala ang particle number at spin-Z conservation para katawanin ang mga state vector nang mas compact kaysa sa generic na $2^n$-dimensional na qubit statevector. Nagtatakda ito ng mga protocol na maaaring ipatupad ng anumang object para makilahok sa simulation machinery nito (tingnan ang [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") para sa sariling mga protocol ng package na ito, na sumusunod sa parehong disenyo):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, applying the object as a unitary to a fixed-particle-number state vector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), sa pamamagitan ng method na `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, na naglalapat sa object bilang unitary sa isang fixed-particle-number na state vector\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, returning a [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") view of the object on that same sector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), sa pamamagitan ng method na `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, na nagbabalik ng [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") na view ng object sa parehong sector na iyon\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, returning the object’s trace on that sector.\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), sa pamamagitan ng method na `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, na nagbabalik ng trace ng object sa sector na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements that interface: every fermionic gate in [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") provides `_apply_unitary_`, and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") provides `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`. That is what makes this package’s operators and circuits *compatible* with ffsim, so its tools work on them natively, with no conversion step. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") can simulate a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") end to end, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") can diagonalize a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), and sampling utilities like [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (used in the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) to turn a simulated statevector into measurement counts) work without modification.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng package na ito ang interface na iyon: bawat fermionic gate sa [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") ay nagbibigay ng `_apply_unitary_`, at ang [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") ay nagbibigay ng `_linear_operator_` at `_trace_`. Iyon ang dahilan kaya *compatible* sa ffsim ang mga operator at circuit ng package na ito, kaya natural na gumagana ang mga tool nito sa kanila, nang walang hakbang ng conversion. Kayang i-simulate ng [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") ang isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") mula simula hanggang dulo, kayang i-diagonalize ng [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") ang isang [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), at gumagana nang walang pagbabago ang mga sampling utility tulad ng [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (ginamit sa [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) para gawing measurement count ang isang na-simulate na statevector).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What `_linear_operator_` returns is an ordinary SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), so [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") and friends work on it too.\n"
msgstr "Ang ibinabalik ng `_linear_operator_` ay isang ordinaryong SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), kaya gumagana rin dito ang [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") at mga kauri nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coupling through ffsim’s protocols is what buys this: its actively developed ecosystem of simulation and sampling utilities applies to this package’s circuits and operators unchanged, and users already working with ffsim can mix in this package’s gates and operators without learning another simulation API.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagkakabit sa pamamagitan ng mga protocol ng ffsim ang nagbibigay nito: ang aktibong nade-develop nitong ecosystem ng mga simulation at sampling utility ay nalalapat nang walang pagbabago sa mga circuit at operator ng package na ito, at maaaring ihalo ng mga user na gumagamit na ng ffsim ang mga gate at operator ng package na ito nang hindi na kailangang matuto ng isa pang simulation API.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is an optional dependency {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"
msgstr "Opsyonal na dependency ang ffsim {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is declared as an optional extra (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, or transitively by `[all]`), guarded at runtime by [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (as was shown above). Installing it unlocks simulation: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") are implemented by converting this package’s [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") into an [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), so without ffsim they raise [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Everything that does not simulate (building operators, mapping them, and transpiling the resulting circuits) needs none of it.\n"
msgstr "Idinedeklara ang ffsim bilang opsyonal na extra (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, o transitively ng `[all]`), na binabantayan sa runtime ng [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (gaya ng ipinakita sa itaas). Ang pag-install nito ang nagbubukas ng simulation: ang [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") at [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") ay ipinapatupad sa pamamagitan ng pag-convert ng [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") ng package na ito sa isang [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), kaya kapag walang ffsim ay nagtataas sila ng [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Lahat ng hindi nagsi-simulate (pagbuo ng mga operator, pag-map sa mga ito, at pag-transpile ng mga nagresultang circuit) ay hindi nangangailangan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fermionic simulation lives in a fixed particle-number sector {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"
msgstr "Nasa fixed particle-number sector ang fermionic simulation {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both `_apply_unitary_` and `_linear_operator_` take an `nelec` argument and represent the state vector over the *fixed-particle-number determinant basis* for that `(norb, nelec)` sector, mirroring ffsim’s (and, transitively, PySCF’s) FCI space setup, rather than the full $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$-dimensional space a general qubit simulator would use. This is a much smaller space (its size is a product of binomial coefficients rather than a power of two), but it comes with a hard restriction. Only operators and gates that preserve particle number (and, in the spinful case, each spin species’ particle number individually) can be represented in it. An operator whose action would move amplitude to a different particle number has nowhere to put it.\n"
msgstr "Parehong kumukuha ng argumentong `nelec` ang `_apply_unitary_` at `_linear_operator_` at kinakatawan ang state vector sa *fixed-particle-number determinant basis* para sa sector na `(norb, nelec)`, na ginagaya ang FCI space setup ng ffsim (at, sa pamamagitan nito, ng PySCF), imbes na ang buong $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$-dimensional na espasyong gagamitin ng isang general na qubit simulator. Mas maliit na espasyo ito nang malaki (ang laki nito ay produkto ng mga binomial coefficient imbes na power ng dalawa), ngunit may kasama itong mahigpit na restriksyon. Mga operator at gate lang na nagpapanatili ng particle number (at, sa spinful na kaso, ng particle number ng bawat spin species nang hiwalay) ang maaaring katawanin dito. Ang operator na ang aksyon ay maglilipat ng amplitude sa ibang particle number ay walang mapaglalagyan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim resolves this by rejecting such an operator outright: converting one to a linear operator raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) naming which conservation law fails. That is the right default, because applying $\\exp(-i t H)$ for a Hamiltonian $H$ with a non-particle-conserving term would otherwise turn a would-be unitary into a non-unitary, physically-meaningless map.\n"
msgstr "Nilulutas ito ng ffsim sa pamamagitan ng tuwirang pagtanggi sa ganoong operator: ang pag-convert ng isa sa linear operator ay nagtataas ng [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) na pinangangalanan kung aling conservation law ang pumapalya. Tamang default iyon, dahil ang paglalapat ng $\\exp(-i t H)$ para sa isang Hamiltonian na $H$ na may term na hindi nagpapanatili ng particle ay gagawing non-unitary at walang pisikal na kahulugang mapa ang dapat sana ay unitary.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") surfaces that rejection from the operator it evolves.\n"
msgstr "Inilalantad ng [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ang pagtanggi na iyon mula sa operator na ine-evolve nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") checks that its (embedded) rotation matrix is block-diagonal across the alpha/beta split in the spinful case, and raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) if it mixes spin sectors.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") na ang (naka-embed na) rotation matrix nito ay block-diagonal sa alpha/beta split sa spinful na kaso, at nagtataas ito ng [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) kung hinahalo nito ang mga spin sector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-particle-preserving simulation is therefore out of reach in fermionic space, by construction of the fixed-sector representation, and that is the price of the compact FCI space which makes fermionic simulation tractable in the first place. If your algorithm needs particle-number-violating operators (for example, a qubit-native error channel, or an operator built for a mapped Hamiltonian that does not conserve particle numbers term by term), transpile to qubits first and simulate the resulting [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) with a qubit-level simulator instead. Any transpilation route works for this; the [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) and [transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guides go into more detail, but [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") is a reasonable default choice.\n"
msgstr "Kaya hindi posible sa fermionic space ang simulation na hindi nagpepreserba ng particle, dahil sa disenyo ng fixed-sector na representasyon, at iyon ang kapalit ng compact na FCI space na siyang nagpapadali sa fermionic simulation sa unang lugar. Kung kailangan ng algorithm mo ang mga operator na lumalabag sa particle-number (halimbawa, isang qubit-native na error channel, o isang operator na binuo para sa mapped Hamiltonian na hindi nagpepreserba ng bilang ng particle sa bawat term), mag-transpile muna sa mga qubit at i-simulate ang nagresultang [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) gamit ang qubit-level na simulator. Gagana ang anumang ruta ng transpilation para dito; mas detalyado ang [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) at [transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) na mga gabay, pero ang [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") ay isang makatwirang default na pagpipilian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The block-spin convention for spinful systems {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"
msgstr "Ang block-spin convention para sa mga spinful na sistema {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`nelec` is typed `int | tuple[int, int]`, and its type, not a separate flag, is what selects one of the supported mode layouts:\n"
msgstr "Ang `nelec` ay may type na `int | tuple[int, int]`, at ang type nito, hindi ang hiwalay na flag, ang pumipili ng isa sa mga sinusuportahang mode layout:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **int** selects the **spinless** interpretation. The `norb` modes are treated directly as spinless orbitals, and `nelec` is the total particle count.\n"
msgstr "Ang **int** ay pumipili ng **spinless** na interpretasyon. Ang `norb` na mga mode ay direktang tinatrato bilang spinless na mga orbital, at ang `nelec` ay ang kabuuang bilang ng particle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **pair** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` selects the **spinful** interpretation of `2 * norb` modes under a fixed **block-spin convention**. Modes `0 .. norb` are the alpha (spin-up) orbitals and modes `norb .. 2 * norb` are the beta (spin-down) orbitals. Each spin species is conserved *independently*; an alpha-only term can move an electron between alpha modes but never into a beta mode, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr "Ang **pair** na `(n_alpha, n_beta)` ay pumipili ng **spinful** na interpretasyon ng `2 * norb` na mga mode sa ilalim ng nakapirming **block-spin convention**. Ang mga mode na `0 .. norb` ay ang mga alpha (spin-up) na orbital at ang mga mode na `norb .. 2 * norb` ay ang mga beta (spin-down) na orbital. Ang bawat spin species ay napepreserba nang *hiwalay*; ang alpha-only na term ay maaaring maglipat ng electron sa pagitan ng mga alpha mode pero hindi kailanman papunta sa beta mode, at vice versa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This dispatch happens at every ffsim-protocol entry point in this package (gate constructors, `_apply_unitary_placed_` implementations, and the native Rust kernel’s sector compilation), and it is the convention used throughout the [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) and [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) guides (for example, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") fills alpha occupations into modes `0 .. n_alpha` and beta occupations into modes `norb .. norb + n_beta`). It is worth contrasting this with the [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") in general, which use *generic* mode indices with no inherent spin semantics (see the [fermionic circuit guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). The block-spin meaning is imposed only when a spinful `nelec` is supplied to a simulation call, not baked into the operator or circuit representation itself.\n"
msgstr "Nangyayari ang dispatch na ito sa bawat ffsim-protocol entry point sa package na ito (mga gate constructor, mga implementasyon ng `_apply_unitary_placed_`, at ang sector compilation ng native Rust kernel), at ito ang convention na ginagamit sa buong [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) at [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) na mga gabay (halimbawa, nilalagay ng [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") ang mga alpha occupation sa mga mode na `0 .. n_alpha` at ang mga beta occupation sa mga mode na `norb .. norb + n_beta`). Makabubuting ihambing ito sa module na [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") at sa [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") sa pangkalahatan, na gumagamit ng *generic* na mga mode index na walang likas na kahulugang spin (tingnan ang [gabay sa fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). Ang kahulugang block-spin ay ipinapataw lamang kapag may ibinigay na spinful na `nelec` sa isang simulation call, at hindi nakabaon sa mismong representasyon ng operator o circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Walk through the [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) guide to see [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") used together to sample circuits built from this package’s gates, and to evaluate a Hamiltonian expectation value through [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") (itself backed by the same `_linear_operator_` protocol method described here).\n"
msgstr "Pag-aralan ang gabay na [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) para makita kung paano ginagamit nang magkasama ang [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") at [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") para mag-sample ng mga circuit na binuo mula sa mga gate ng package na ito, at para i-evaluate ang expectation value ng Hamiltonian sa pamamagitan ng [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") (na sinusuportahan din ng parehong `_linear_operator_` protocol method na inilarawan dito).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
